{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l2rnww7b","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline","year":2011,"examDate":2011,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"hydrocarbons","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"properties-and-preparation-of-alkenes","type":"integer","marks":3,"negMarks":0,"permalink":"pthe-total-number-of-alkenes-possible-by-dehydrobrominatio-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-j8idzwjycfzpjgwy","content":"<p>The total number of alkenes possible by dehydrobromination of 3-bromo-3-cyclopentylhexane using alcoholic KOH is _______.</p>","options":[],"correct_options":[],"explanation":"(1) The structure of 3-bromo-3-cyclopentylhexane -\n<br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lh4qs3bg/37084bb5-0302-4e8b-b01b-48367402ea9e/2892f0c0-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qs3bh.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lh4qs3bg/37084bb5-0302-4e8b-b01b-48367402ea9e/2892f0c0-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qs3bh.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Hydrocarbons Question 16 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lh4qs3bg/37084bb5-0302-4e8b-b01b-48367402ea9e/2892f0c0-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qs3bh.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lh4qs3bg/37084bb5-0302-4e8b-b01b-48367402ea9e/2892f0c0-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qs3bh.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lh4qs3bg/37084bb5-0302-4e8b-b01b-48367402ea9e/2892f0c0-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qs3bh.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lh4qs3bg/37084bb5-0302-4e8b-b01b-48367402ea9e/2892f0c0-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qs3bh.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lh4qs3bg/37084bb5-0302-4e8b-b01b-48367402ea9e/2892f0c0-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qs3bh.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lh4qs3bg/37084bb5-0302-4e8b-b01b-48367402ea9e/2892f0c0-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qs3bh.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n<br><br>(2) Since, bromide (Br<sup>–</sup>) is a good leaving group,\nelimination using strong base takes place using\nstrong base (KOH) take via E<sub>2</sub> mechanism.\nThis is also called <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"2.034ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 573 899\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D6FD\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D6FD\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> elimination.\n<br><br>(3) There are 3 different types of protons :\n<br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lh4qwq76/7ba176d5-e6fd-4c54-81a0-df91096373ea/a97c5820-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qwq77.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lh4qwq76/7ba176d5-e6fd-4c54-81a0-df91096373ea/a97c5820-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qwq77.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2011 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Hydrocarbons Question 16 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lh4qwq76/7ba176d5-e6fd-4c54-81a0-df91096373ea/a97c5820-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qwq77.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lh4qwq76/7ba176d5-e6fd-4c54-81a0-df91096373ea/a97c5820-e811-11ed-8e58-b75ca46f959b/file-1lh4qwq77.png?format=png 750w, https